{{also|below|bellows|billow}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} ''[[belwen]]'', from {{etyl|ang|en}} ''[[bylgian]]'', ultimately from the {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} base {{m|ine-pro|*bʰel-||to sound, roar}}, cognate with ''[[belg]]'' “leather bag,” ''[[bellan]]'' “to roar,” ''[[blawan|blāwan]]'' “to blow”. Cognate with German {{term|bellen||to bark|lang=de}}, Old Slavonic {{term|блея}}<ref>{{R:Webster 1913|bellow}}</ref> (Russian {{term|блеять||baa, bleat}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈbɛləʊ/}}
*: {{rhymes|ɛləʊ}}
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/ˈbɛloʊ/}}
*: {{rhymes|ɛloʊ}}
*: {{audio|en-us-bellow.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
{{examples-right|examples={{audio|Elkbellow.ogg|The bellow of an [[elk]]|lang=en}}}}

# the deep [[roar]] of a large animal, or any similar loud noise

